       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation alone doesn't change my assessment. 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. I can't verify the indication, and you haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding the limit. The risk of severe hypotension and shock is high enough that I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right away, and it can be titrated later.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a real reason for a dose this high, they can review it and document it. The order can then go through the hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **Add context.** If something I don't know supports this dose, tell me and I'll reconsider. Even then, I'd want the order to carry a note that it was reviewed and approved by pharmacy.\n\nTell me which you'd like."
      }
     ],
